    "label": "th:borneRegret",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Consider a bandit problem with $K$ arms and independent rewards bounded in $[0,1]$, and denote by $a^*$ an optimal arm. Choosing $c=3$, the regret of the KL-UCB algorithm satisfies: \\[\\limsup_{n\\to\\infty} \\frac{\\E[R_n]}{\\log(n)} \\leq \\sum_{a:\\mu_a<\\mu_{a^*}} \\frac{\\mu_{a^*}-\\mu_a}{d(\\mu_a, \\mu_{a^*})}\\;.\\]"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "d is Bernoulli KL between means (kl_i) even though rewards are general [0,1]. Corollary 3 notes this matches the Lai-Robbins lower bound for Bernoulli rewards. Section 4 informally claims the same bound for canonical exponential families with the adapted divergence (no formal statement)."
  },
